  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-20T01:12:56.198Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When checking what groups I'm in are active, I find it frustrating having to click \"Groups\" and then \"Group Activity\" to find what I'm looking for.\n\nI understand that \"Explore Groups\" is likely the default to encourage new users to find groups, but I feel like this could be accomplished by simply making \"Group Activity\" default but directing the player towards group discovery if they aren't in any groups/no active instances are being displayed.\n\nI think this would make the experience of hopping on and checking what certain groups are up to a lot smoother.",
